    "known_gaps": {
      "uplift_is_an_estimate": "1.34 is one owner's impression from customer remarks, in one suburb, at one shop. The low end of every range is verified; the top end is not. This is the single weakest number in this file and the page must say so."
    },
    "price_decay": "PRICE only. Refurbished-original screens fall in price for ~2 years post-launch, then flatten. Genuine new original holds its price indefinitely. The $750-850 refurb figure for a 17 Pro Max was true at launch and stale nine months later. Re-verify the 'current' band every 6 months.",
    "refurb_quality": "A refurbished original IS the original panel. The same OLED is reclaimed and re-laminated with new glass and adhesive. Performance is equivalent to a genuine new part. The saving comes from reclaiming the panel, not from a lesser component. NEVER imply refurbished parts degrade or wear out.",
    "shop_range_method": "Published screen range = [anchor-shop low, anchor-shop high x 1.34]. LOW END: verified retail from one independent shop in Newcastle NSW. TOP END: ESTIMATE ONLY. Derived from that owner's recollection of customer remarks that his prices run 20-30% below others. Not surveyed, not sampled, not measured. Do NOT present the top of the range as a shopping-centre price, a big-city price, or any other specific kind of shop. Rent and location may explain the spread; that is a hypothesis from one operator, not a finding. Batteries carry no uplift.",
    "shop_range_uplift": {
      "all_brands_screens": 1.34,
      "batteries": 1
    },
    "price_advantage": "Independent shops are dramatically cheaper than Apple on the incell and aftermarket-OLED tiers, which is where most customers land. On refurbished-OEM they are at or ABOVE Apple's out-of-warranty price on most models. On that tier the reasons to use a shop are not price: no factory wipe, no booking wait, same-day turnaround, local access.",
    "tier_availability": {
      "apple_oled": [
        "incell",
        "aft_oled",
        "refurb_oem",
        "genuine_special_order"
      ],
      "apple_lcd": [
        "incell",
        "oem_lcd"
      ],
      "samsung_s": [
        "oem_or_refurb"
      ],
      "samsung_a": [
        "incell",
        "oem_or_refurb"
      ],
      "samsung_z_fold_flip": [
        "oem_or_refurb"
      ],
      "samsung_note": [
        "oem_or_refurb"
      ],
      "pixel": [
        "oem_or_refurb"
      ]
    },
    "tier_availability_note": "Apple is the only brand with a budget repair market: incell AND aftermarket OLED both exist. Galaxy A has incell only. Galaxy S, Note, foldables and Pixel have neither - one tier, and it's the expensive one. Refurbished originals DO exist for Samsung and Pixel, but sit close enough to new OEM that they are not priced separately. Curved/edge panels are the hardest to refurbish, which is why they carry the smallest refurb discount.",
    "foldable_note": "Z Fold / Z Flip: inner and outer screens are separate parts and separate prices. Two rows each.",
    "android_band_key": "For Samsung and Pixel the price driver is PANEL GEOMETRY (flat vs curved/edge) and size, NOT model age. A Pixel 7 Pro costs more than a Pixel 9 because it is curved. An S Ultra costs ~$100 more than an S base for the same reason. Do not sort these bands by year.",
    "publishing_rules": [
      "State that the low end comes from one verified AU shop and the top end is an estimate.",
      "Do not attribute the spread to rent, shop type, or city without evidence.",
      "Do not describe any tier as lower quality. Refurbished originals ARE the original panel.",
      "Do not claim independent shops are cheaper than the manufacturer across the board. True on incell and aftermarket OLED. Not true on OEM for most models.",
      "Date every row. Re-verify current-generation rows every 6 months."
    ],
    "quote_required_policy": "A row with quote_required MUST still render, with its model name, its available tiers, and a clear 'ask for a quote' call to action. It must never render a price, an estimate, or a dash. These rows exist to be found in search, not to be filled in later."
  },
